{{!
    @template core/permissionmanager_panelcontent

    Inner content of the "Allow role" / "Prohibit role" dialogue on the permissions page.

    Retani: the message, then the roles as a list of full-width rows (like the file picker's
    repository list). Roles already in the list are shown disabled with "Added".
    The permission manager JS (core/permissionmanager) listens for clicks on the buttons with
    data-role-id inside div.role_buttons, so both stay.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * message Confirmation text
    * roles array of role details. Note: in this array, rolename must have been
          prepared for output with format_string, or more likely one of the role API functions like role_fix_names.

    Example context (json):
    { "message": "Select a role to be added to the list of allowed roles in context \"Course: Design 101\", capability \"View added and updated modules in recent activity block\":",
      "roles": [{"roleid": 1, "rolename": "Manager", "disabled": "disabled"}, {"roleid": 3, "rolename": "Teacher", "disabled": ""}]}
}}
<div class="popup_content retani-rolepicker">
    <p class="retani-rolepicker-message">{{message}}</p>
    <div class="role_buttons retani-rolepicker-list">
        {{#roles}}
            <button type="button" class="retani-rolepicker-role" data-role-id="{{roleid}}" {{disabled}}>
                <span class="retani-rolepicker-name">{{{rolename}}}</span>
                <span class="retani-rolepicker-state retani-rolepicker-added">{{#str}}rolepicker:added, theme_retani_studio{{/str}}</span>
                <span class="retani-rolepicker-state retani-rolepicker-add" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
                </span>
            </button>
        {{/roles}}
    </div>
</div>
